  <result aggregation-status="0" type="2">
   <title>
    <narrative xml:lang="EN">Output 3.4. Increased capacity of ILO constituents to promote peaceful, stable and resilient societies through decent work</narrative>
   </title>
   <description>
    <narrative xml:lang="EN">In the framework of National Strategy for Gender Equality 2012-2020 and its National Action Plan 2018-2020, the Ministry of Health and Social Development of the Kyrgyz Republic initiated the implementation of measures to promote an enabling environment for decent work and economic empowerment of women to tackle fragility drivers in conflict-prone settings. A technical working group was created to ensure implementation of Chapter 1 - Economic empowerment of women - and Goals 1.1 - Creation of conditions necessary for ensuring decent work for women - and 1.2 - Promoting the employment of women. ILO training programs - GET Ahead, Financial Education, and Start and Improve Your Business - were adopted as a result of tripartite consultations and cooperation with MHSD, the National Bank of Kyrgyz Republic and business associations. Implementation of these gender-responsive training programmes - on skills development, employment opportunities, decent work, labour rights, corporate social responsibility - contribute to building resilience and social cohesion and mitigating factors of instability, including effects of migration and COVID-19, in four regions of Kyrgyzstan. As a result, greater socio-economic opportunities for women and girls affected by migration were created, their employability and access to decent income and jobs strengthened. With increased capacities, national partners, social partners, and business associations will continue using and replicating these training programmes in other regions of Kyrgyzstan to promote peaceful society through decent work. The ILO supported a joint entrepreneurship training using the &quot;Do No Harm&quot; approach and information on business continuity management. Overall, 358 people (351 women and 7 men) attended online GET Ahead training; 269  women and girls received additional support of increased access to economic opportunities (technical training, master-classes, exchange visits, individual consultations). Out of them, 151  women benefitted from the ILO SYB training in September 2021 to develop business plans.
 
The ILO Financial Education e-learning course was conducted in Kyrgyz and Russian in collaboration with ITC-ILO Turin; 14 trainers were certified and conducted online trainings on financial education to women and girls affected by migration and their family members. In total, 24 training sessions were held for 308 people (258 women, 50 men) from municipalities of Ak-Turpak, Orozbekov, Toolos, Bel, Kara-Buura, Kyzyl-Tuu. As of July 2021, 250 women and girls and their family members completed the course and got online certificates. The ILO implementation partner - Public Found Association of Trainers &amp; Consultants (PF ATiC) - developed and conducted follow-up consulting services for the women and girls and their family members.</narrative>
   </description>
   <indicator aggregation-status="0" measure="5">
